      "copyCitation": "U.S. Department of State, Embassy Santo Domingo, telegram 1990 SANTO 006676, “U.S.-LATIN AMERICA RELATIONS IN THE ERA OF PERESTROIKA AND GLASNOST,” 1990-06-01, FOIA Library, case M-2014-23169, document C09000027, source PDF, pp. 1–5.",
      "summary": "Ambassador Paul Taylor responds to an invitation to comment on U.S.–Latin American relations, proposing comprehensive hemispheric free trade and recommending that the Caribbean be an early trading bloc.",
      "relevance": "Directly relevant to Volume XXX’s Foreign Economic Policy scope: the Ambassador’s cable to ARA proposes a hemispheric free-trade strategy, discusses the Caribbean Basin Initiative, and frames trade and aid as tools of U.S. economic policy.",
